# Proposals change the rules the next run is constrained by.
# GitHub requests this review on a pull request someone else opens. It blocks
# a merge only once branch protection on main requires code owner review.
# Merging a proposal does not apply it.
/proposals/ @tounsoo
# A proposal that only adds is adopted in the pull request that adds it, so
# this review is its only approval. This line covers any folder named
# proposals. A product whose paths.proposals names a folder with another
# name needs its own line here.
proposals/ @tounsoo
# Each product under products/ has a harness config that says where every
# inventory lives. Changing a path can empty a check, so it needs a proposal
# and the same review.
/products/*/harness.config.ts @tounsoo
# An approved pattern is adopted into the harness as a check that applies to
# every product, so a designer reviews every change to the harness.
/packages/harness/ @tounsoo
# check:rules in package.json is the list of rules every product follows, so
# taking a rule out of it is a retirement and needs the same review.
/package.json @tounsoo
# The design system adapter names the parts every check counts. Swapping a
# name can empty a check the same way.
/packages/adapter-todae/ @tounsoo
# CI names the config each product job checks. Pointing a job at another
# config file would check a product against an inventory with no base.
/.github/workflows/ @tounsoo
